Modifications
-------------

Changes made in this fork, relative to upstream (AGPL-3.0 section 5a requires
that modifications be marked):

  2026-08  Added a test suite and fixed the defects it found, including an
           unbounded loop reachable from the graph-build endpoint and a JSON
           repair routine that corrupted valid input.
  2026-08  Added an access-key layer with credit metering, subscriptions and
           one-off top-ups, plus Stripe checkout and webhook fulfilment.
  2026-08  Added multi-tenant isolation: projects, simulations, reports,
           crowds, predictions and build tasks are scoped to the key that
           created them.
  2026-08  Added reusable crowds, a calibration record, and an operator
           console.
  2026-08  Rebranded the user-facing product from MiroFish to SpiderNet, and
           translated the interface and generated output to English.

Renaming the product does not change its licence or its origin.


If you run this over a network
------------------------------

AGPL-3.0 section 13 requires that anyone interacting with this software
remotely be offered its Corresponding Source, at no charge.

Deployments must therefore publish the source of the exact version they run,
including any local modifications, and link to it from the running
application. SpiderNet does this through GET /api/legal/source and a link in
the interface; set SOURCE_URL to point at your own repository before
deploying, or that offer points somewhere that does not match what you are
running.


